meta {
  name: Leave the group
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

delete {
  url: {{groupService}}/members
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "groupKey": "{{groupKey}}",
    "memberSecret": "{{memberSecret}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("reports whether there was a lease to release", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.memberId).to.be.a("string");
    expect(res.body.released).to.be.a("boolean");
  });
}

docs {
  # Leave the group

  Drops this member's presence, which is what closing the app does without waiting the lease out.

  Idempotent: a member holding no lease is already in the state this names, so a second call answers `released: false` and is a success.

  It reconciles afterwards, which closes what the leaver held while anybody else in the group still holds a lease.
  Where the leaver was the last live member the group stops being enforced instead, and what they hold is left alone until somebody states presence again: a group nobody has stated presence in looks exactly like an app that has not stated its own yet.
}
